As part of a research project, doctors and scientists investigated the effect of altitude on the ability of blood to carry oxygen. They assessed changes in the oxygen-carrying ability of their own blood as they walked from 1530 m above sea level to 5700 m above sea level over 14 days. 5700 m is an extremely high altitude.

Table 4.1 is a summary of some of their results.

